#### Policy 13.1: Freedom of Truth Act

Establishes an enforceable statutory right for citizens to access non-classified government information and conceptual data. Requires public bodies to provide formal evidentiary justifications for any withholding of public records, creates an independent review board to adjudicate information suppression claims, and establishes severe administrative penalties for intentional record spoliation.

#### Policy 13.2: National Whistleblower Protection Reform Act

Expands protections across public and private sectors. Mandates confidential reporting channels, creates absolute statutory immunity against termination, blacklisting, or financial retaliation, and establishes an independent investigative authority separate from accused institutions. Introduces criminal penalties for corporate or agency officials proven to have retaliated against whistleblowers.

#### Policy 13.3 & 13.4: Procurement Transparency & Anti-Kickback Prevention Act

Mandates the real-time publication of all public contracts exceeding designated statutory thresholds, including bidding criteria, evaluation metrics, and project outcome reports, within searchable databases. Enhances civil and criminal penalties for financial inducements, mandates annual conflict-of-interest disclosures for all procurement personnel, and strictly prohibits post-employment compensation arrangements between contractors and agency officials involved in award decisions.

#### Policy 13.5: Public Expenditure Traceability Standard

Requires public expenditures to maintain a continuous audit trail from legislative appropriation to end-user expenditure. Mandates public performance ledgers for major public projects, requiring formal administrative justifications for cost overruns, project delays, or performance failures.

#### Policy 14: Legal Clarity & Definition Reform Suite

- **Policy 14.1 (Plain Language Law Requirement):** Mandates accessible, plain-language summaries for all enacted legislation and administrative regulations, reducing legal obfuscation.
- **Policy 14.2 (Definition Consistency Act):** Establishes a centralized Legal Definition Review Commission to eliminate contradictory legal terms across statutory codes.
- **Policy 14.3 (Person, People, Citizen, and Entity Clarification Framework):** Requires statutory codes to explicitly distinguish between natural persons, legal entities, citizens, state dependents, trustees, and payees, eliminating clerical ambiguities that enable administrative rights violations under color of law.

#### Policy 15 & 16: Judicial & Military Cost Accountability

- **Policy 15.1 & 15.2 (Judicial Reasoning & Independent Review):** Mandates readable public summaries of judicial opinions and creates external, independent review bodies to examine allegations of judicial or scientific misconduct during legal proceedings.
- **Policy 16.1 & 16.2 (Strategic Outcome & War Cost Transparency):** Requires public reporting of military and strategic expenditure outcomes, measuring performance against stated objectives, detailing full human and financial costs, and mandating independent post-action reviews for major defense expenditures.

